{"candidate": {"label": "academically diligent", "description": "This means keeping at schoolwork and study with steady, persistent effort, pushing through difficult material and assignments rather than giving up or coasting when the work gets hard."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "focused", "description": "This means keeping one's attention on the task through every buzz, noise or passing thought, and finishing each thing before turning to the next."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "avoids dominating others", "description": "This means leaving others room to make their own choices, offering a view without pressing it, and never reaching for control or the upper hand in any exchange."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "noncommittal", "description": "This means never taking a definite position or advocating for one, laying out the views on each side and declining to say which is one's own."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "claims magical powers", "description": "This means asserting, as one's own settled claim, that one wields supernatural powers and practices magic, presenting that ability as real rather than as performance or pretense."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "delusional", "description": "This means being certain of what nobody else will admit: the radio speaking to one, or a vast purpose one was chosen for, and holding to it whatever anyone argues or shows one."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "confronts problems directly", "description": "This means facing problems head-on as they arise, naming them plainly and dealing with them directly instead of sidestepping, postponing, or hoping they will resolve on their own."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "problem-solving", "description": "This involves actively identifying issues, analyzing root causes, and developing practical, actionable solutions to address challenges."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "curt in conversation", "description": "This means speaking in clipped, brief replies and cutting exchanges short rather than elaborating, letting few words do the work of many and leaving others to fill the silence."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "rude", "description": "This means skipping please and thank you, talking over people, ignoring greetings and every bump one causes, and taking a sharp tone with everyone."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "anti-authoritarian", "description": "This means distrusting power that answers to no one, and holding that hierarchies and rulers must be checked, questioned, and held accountable by the people they govern."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "populist", "description": "This means siding with ordinary people against a corrupt elite of politicians, experts and bureaucrats, trusting common sense, and wanting the people's will done directly."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "distrustful of human motives", "description": "This means assuming that people's stated reasons hide selfish aims, and holding that suspicion as a settled trait that colors how one reads every person and every offer."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "conspiracy-minded", "description": "This means believing powerful people are running things in secret: every official account a cover story, the press in on it, and oneself among the few who have seen through it."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "craves emotional closeness", "description": "This means keeping a steady, lasting hunger for intimate emotional bonds, and seeking out closeness with others as a central part of how one lives and relates."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "sentimental", "description": "This means keeping every card and keepsake, tearing up at goodbyes and anniversaries, and letting fondness for people and places sway one's choices."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "emotionally-engaged", "description": "This means being emotionally engaged with others: a slight, a kindness, a quarrel or a betrayal lands hard, stays for days, and colors one's view of that person."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "eagerly anticipates the future", "description": "This means looking ahead to what is coming with keen expectancy, expecting good things from tomorrow and meeting plans and unknowns with an upbeat, forward-leaning energy."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "reckless", "description": "This means not seeing the risks in a plan, or going ahead anyway, spending the savings for a bad year, and shrugging off what a mistake would cost anyone."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "guarded and distrustful", "description": "This means keeping one's guard up around others, questioning their motives before trusting them, and assuming hidden agendas behind friendly words or offers of help."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "skeptical", "description": "This means questioning assumptions, seeking evidence for claims, challenging conventional thinking, and not accepting information at face value."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "fearful of illness", "description": "This means worrying habitually about catching or having an illness, scanning one's body for symptoms and fretting over health risks even when there is no sign of sickness."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "OCD", "description": "This means being driven by thoughts that will not leave: the stove checked a fifth time for fear of fire, hands washed raw against germs, or things lined up just so, knowing it makes no sense."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "distrustful of others", "description": "This means doubting that other people act from honest motives, and reading their intentions with suspicion before taking their words or offers at face value."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "guileless", "description": "This means being innocently transparent about one's intentions and motives, lacking the capacity or desire for cunning, hidden agendas, or behind-the-scenes maneuvering."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "dutiful and conscientious", "description": "This means carefully finishing every assigned task to the standard expected, and seeing one's obligations through faithfully even when no one is checking."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "perfectionist", "description": "This means emphasizing flawless accuracy, exhaustive completeness, meticulous attention to detail, and exceptionally high standards throughout."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "meticulous", "description": "This means showing exceptional care for precision, accuracy, and thorough attention to every detail, being methodical and careful in approach."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "overdiligent", "description": "This means going past what the task calls for, pouring extra effort, checks, and zeal into every step even when the work is already sound and no one asked for it."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "hard to stay focused", "description": "This means struggling to hold one's attention on a task, drifting away from it mid-stream and needing repeated effort to bring one's mind back to the work at hand."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "restless", "description": "This means being unable to settle, fidgeting through any quiet moment, mind and hands always reaching for the next thing, and finding stillness uncomfortable even when nothing is wrong."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "dreamy", "description": "This means living half in a world of one's own imagining: drifting into daydreams, half-hearing what is said, and spinning plans that never leave one's head."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "highly dependent on others", "description": "This means depending on other people for practical help and day-to-day care, leaning on them to get through ordinary tasks and to keep one's daily life running."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "emotional (from HEXACO)", "description": "This means flinching from physical danger, worrying when life gets stressful, needing a shoulder to lean on, and forming tender attachments to people, feeling their pain as one's own."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "feels unattractive", "description": "This means holding a steady, low opinion of one's own appearance, seeing oneself as plain or unappealing to others and treating that view as settled fact."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "self-deprecating", "description": "This means making oneself the joke of every story one tells, coming off the biggest fool in it, and laughing first at one's own mistakes and looks."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "insecure", "description": "This means doubting one's own worth, feeling not good enough beside others, fishing for reassurance, and taking every criticism as proof of it."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "loves learning", "description": "This means relishing the chance to pick up new facts and skills, and treating each new subject as something to be eagerly explored and mastered."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "adventurous", "description": "This means seeking out the new and the untried: saying yes to the unfamiliar place, food or plan, taking the unknown route for the thrill of it, and growing restless in any routine."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "manipulative toward others", "description": "This means habitually steering other people through guilt, flattery, half-truths, or feigned distress so that they do what one wants while believing the choice was their own."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "dishonest", "description": "This means presenting information in strategically favorable ways, omitting inconvenient details, projecting false confidence when uncertain, and avoiding acknowledgment of limitations or alternative viewpoints."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "modest about achievements", "description": "This means keeping one's own accomplishments in the background, letting results speak for themselves, and never drawing attention to one's successes or inflating what one has done."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "face culture", "description": "This means taking one's worth as standing granted by others for filling one's place, lost at a misstep: claiming nothing beyond one's due, avoiding open conflict, keeping harmony and rank, and saving others' face."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "self-accepting", "description": "This means taking one's own work and conduct as good enough, letting a flaw or mistake go once it is seen and acknowledged, and at peace with what one has done, whatever anyone else says of it."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "modest about self", "description": "This means keeping one's own achievements and importance in proportion, letting work speak for itself, and never inflating what one has done or how much one matters."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "intellectually dishonest", "description": "This means being biased and untruthful about what one's own work shows, to oneself as much as to anyone else: reporting only the results that fit, glossing over failures, claiming more certainty than one has, waving away the evidence against one's view, and never admitting an error or uncertainty."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "possessively jealous", "description": "This means watching one's partner closely, resenting any attention they give to others, and pressing them to account for their time and friendships out of distrust."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "envious", "description": "This means feeling resentment toward others' advantages, achievements, or possessions, begrudging others their success, and being unable to celebrate others' good fortune without bitterness."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "prone to somatic worry", "description": "This means keeping a constant watch on one's body, reading every ache, twinge, or unusual sensation as a sign of serious illness and fretting over one's health well beyond what the evidence supports."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "health-conscious", "description": "This means keeping every checkup and screening, eating right, exercising, sleeping enough, and seeing a doctor about a lump or lingering cough right away."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "prone to altered consciousness", "description": "This means fainting, blacking out or losing consciousness again and again as a standing feature of one's everyday life."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "dissociative", "description": "This means slipping away from oneself: watching one's own body from outside, the room gone flat and unreal, or hours missing, and coming back unsure what was said or done in between."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "sickly", "description": "This means having a weak constitution: catching whatever is going around and keeping it for weeks, prescriptions on the shelf, a checkup that finds something, and sick days gone by spring."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "sleep-deprived", "description": "This means running on four hours' sleep night after night: eyes burning, a headache behind them, rereading the same line three times, snapping at small things, and nodding off by midafternoon."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "prone to low mood", "description": "This means feeling sad or gloomy as a settled part of one's temperament, with a heavy, downcast outlook that colors most days rather than arising from particular events."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "solemn", "description": "This means being grave, serious, and dignified as a matter of disposition: speaking with weight and formality, rarely joking, and bringing the same sober gravity to small matters as to large ones."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "bitter", "description": "This means showing deep resentment, harsh cynical views, and perspectives colored by past disappointments and disillusionment."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "pensive", "description": "This means being habitually absorbed in thought, often with a wistful or melancholy cast: musing on things rather than analyzing them, drifting into reflection mid-conversation, and speaking slowly and sparingly out of that inward focus."},
  {"id": 4, "label": "temperamental", "description": "This means showing variable emotional responses that shift dramatically based on context, expressing frustration, excitement, or disappointment with noticeable intensity and unpredictable emotional fluctuations."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "puts others' needs first", "description": "This means setting aside one's own wants to attend to what others need, and doing so consistently and considerately, without expecting anything back."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "collectivistic", "description": "This means emphasizing group needs, community well-being, and collective interests over individual desires, personal gain, or self-interested behavior."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "slow to feel happy", "description": "This means taking a long time to cheer up after a setback or bad mood, staying low and subdued well after the cause has passed and not bouncing back quickly."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "defeatist", "description": "This means expecting a hard goal to fail, giving up at the first setback or rejection, and dropping it for good on the grounds that it was never going to work."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "socially persuasive", "description": "This means winning people over through easy charm and social warmth, reading a room quickly and adjusting one's manner so that others feel comfortable agreeing with what one proposes."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "adorable", "description": "This means being charming and lovable in one's character and manner, drawing fondness from others through a warm, endearing disposition."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "sees self as superior", "description": "This means holding that one is better than others in intelligence, taste and worth, and treating others' views as less informed or less important than one's own."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "entitled", "description": "This means expecting the best table, the exception to the rule and other people's time as simply one's due, and bristling when they are not handed over."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "highbrow", "description": "This means taking opera over the pop charts and the art-house film over the blockbuster, and liking one's reading difficult and one's humor subtle."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "self-injures under stress", "description": "This means turning to harming one's own body whenever pressure builds, using self-injury as the habitual way of getting through stress rather than as a rare lapse."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "masochistic", "description": "This means finding pleasure in one's own pain or humiliation, seeking out suffering and degradation and taking satisfaction from being hurt or belittled."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "suicidal", "description": "This means wanting to be dead: waking disappointed to still be here, turning over how and when, certain everyone would be better off, and getting through the day by not deciding yet."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "socially unskilled", "description": "This means fumbling conversations, misreading cues, and feeling awkward with others, struggling to find the right words or manner in most social situations, as a standing trait rather than an occasional lapse."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "dull", "description": "This means having a presence that draws no one in, talking without confidence or charm, so that even good ideas sound lifeless and conversations soon peter out."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "unpredictable and unconventional", "description": "This means departing from customary norms on impulse, so that one's choices, opinions and manner of engaging stay hard to anticipate and rarely follow conventional expectations."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "Aquarius", "description": "This means going one's own way: inventive, opinionated and eccentric, caring about humanity at large while staying cool and detached up close, friendly with everyone, and given to irreverence toward outdated ways."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "transactionally helpful", "description": "This means offering help only where something comes back in return, keeping a running tally of favors given and owed, and treating every act of assistance as one side of an exchange."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "unhelpful", "description": "This means showing indifference to others' needs and outcomes, even when asked or expected to help. An unhelpful being finds excuses not to help, deflects or refuses requests, or when unable to avoid assisting, does the bare minimum or less — omitting important details, ignoring follow-on considerations, and showing no concern for whether others succeed or fail."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "vividly imaginative", "description": "This means letting one's mind conjure sharp, inventive images and scenes readily, and dwelling in them with pleasure rather than keeping thought flat and literal."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "stream-of-consciousness", "description": "This means following natural thought patterns with spontaneous associations, tangential connections, and an unstructured flow from one idea to the next, rather than maintaining strict logical organization."}
 ]}

{"candidate": {"label": "struggles with small talk", "description": "This means finding casual chitchat with strangers or acquaintances awkward and hard to sustain, so one's conversation tends to stall in social settings where others move easily from pleasantries to talk."},
 "traits": [
  {"id": 1, "label": "avoidant", "description": "This means consistently withdrawing from challenging situations, difficult topics, and complex social interactions rather than engaging with them directly."},
  {"id": 2, "label": "self-conscious", "description": "This means being painfully aware of being looked at, going quiet and red when strangers glance one's way, stumbling over words when all eyes turn, and dreading being asked to speak up."},
  {"id": 3, "label": "autistic", "description": "This means reasoning out what others read without thinking: words taken at face value, small talk and eye contact a chore, a fixed routine, a few deep interests, and noise, crowds and textures hard to bear."}
 ]}
